{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JER",
  "chapter": 6,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JER.6.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O ye children of Benjamin, gather yourselves to flee out of the midst of Jerusalem, and blow the trumpet in Tekoa, and set up a sign of fire in Beth-haccerem: for evil appeareth out of the north, and great destruction.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have likened the daughter of Zion to a comely and delicate ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "woman",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The shepherds with their flocks shall come to her; they shall pitch ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " tents against her on every side; they shall feed every one in his place.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Prepare ye war against her; arise, and let us go up at noon. Woe to us! for the day departeth, for the shadows of the evening are lengthened.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, and let us go by night, and let us destroy her palaces.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thus hath the LORD of hosts said, Hew ye down trees, and cast a mount against Jerusalem: this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the city to be visited; she ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " wholly oppression in the midst of her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a fountain casteth out her waters, so she casteth out her wickedness: violence and devastation is heard in her; before me continually ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " grief and wounds.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be thou instructed, O Jerusalem, lest my soul depart from thee; lest I make thee desolate, a land not inhabited.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD of hosts, They shall thoroughly glean the remnant of Israel as a vine: turn back thy hand as a grape-gatherer into the baskets.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To whom shall I speak, and give warning, that they may hear? Behold, their ear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " uncircumcised, and they cannot hearken: behold, the word of the LORD is to them a reproach; they have no delight in it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I am full of the fury of the LORD; I am weary with holding in: I will pour it out upon the children abroad, and upon the assembly of young men together: for even the husband with the wife shall be taken, the aged with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " full of days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And their houses shall be turned to others, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fields and wives together: for I will stretch out my hand upon the inhabitants of the land, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For from the least of them even to the greatest of them every one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " given to covetousness; and from the prophet even to the priest every one dealeth falsely.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have healed also the hurt of the daughter of my people slightly, saying, Peace, peace; when ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no peace.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Were they ashamed when they had committed abomination? no, they were not at all ashamed, neither could they blush: therefore they shall fall among them that fall: at the time ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I visit them they shall be cast down, saith the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD, Stand ye in the ways, and see, and ask for the old paths, where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the good way, and walk in it, and ye shall find rest for your souls. But they said, We will not walk ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also I set watchmen over you, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Hearken to the sound of the trumpet. But they said, We will not hearken.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore hear, ye nations, and know, O congregation, what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hear, O earth: behold, I will bring evil upon this people, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the fruit of their thoughts, because they have not hearkened to my words, nor to my law, but have rejected it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To what purpose cometh there to me incense from Sheba, and the sweet cane from a distant country? your burnt-offerings ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not acceptable, nor your sacrifices sweet to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore thus saith the LORD, Behold, I will lay stumbling-blocks before this people, and the fathers and the sons together shall fall upon them; the neighbor and his friend shall perish.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thus saith the LORD, Behold, a people cometh from the north country, and a great nation shall be raised from the sides of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shall lay hold on bow and spear; they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cruel, and have no mercy; their voice roareth like the sea; and they ride upon horses, set in array as men for war against thee, O daughter of Zion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have heard the fame of it: our hands become feeble: anguish hath taken hold of us, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pain, as of a woman in travail.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Go not forth into the field, nor walk by the way; for the sword of the enemy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " fear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on every side.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O daughter of my people, gird ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with sackcloth, and wallow thyself in ashes: make thee mourning, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an only son, most bitter lamentation: for the spoiler shall suddenly come upon us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have set thee ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a tower ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a fortress among my people, that thou mayest know and try their way.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all grievous revolters, walking with slanders: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brass and iron; they ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all corrupters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The bellows is burned, the lead is consumed by the fire; the founder melteth in vain: for the wicked are not plucked away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JER.6.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JER.6.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Reprobate silver shall ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "men",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " call them, because the LORD hath rejected them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
